module

public import Linglib.Core.Data.List.Infix
public import Linglib.Syntax.Command

/-!
# Projection from heads

Every phrase-structure framework designates in each headed constituent one daughter as its head,
and a phrase is a projection of the head reached from it through head daughters. The frameworks
differ in how they find the head daughter, so here a head relation `H` is a parameter, `H m d`
saying that `d` is the head daughter of `m`. The levels of projection are derived, as relational
properties of nodes rather than parts of their labels: a node is a maximal projection when it is
no node's head daughter and a minimal projection when it has no head daughter.

Adjunction makes no new category. The head relation splits into projection `P` and adjunction
`A`, where `A m d` says that `m` is a further segment of the category of its host `d`, as in May's
multimembered projections and Chomsky's two-segment categories. A category dominates what all its
segments dominate and excludes what none of them dominates, a category is maximal when no segment
of it projects further, and Barker and Pullum's MAX-command is generated by the maximal
categories, each read at its lowest segment. Without adjunction these are the maximal
projections, and an adjunct to a maximal category commands out of it.

On the positions of a rose tree a head relation is given by the index of each position's head
daughter, which makes projection, the levels, categories and the maximal projection decidable.

## Main definitions

* `PhraseStructure.IsProjectionOf`: the reflexive-transitive closure of the head relation.
* `PhraseStructure.IsMaximalProjection`, `PhraseStructure.IsMinimalProjection`,
  `PhraseStructure.IsLexicalHeadOf`.
* `PhraseStructure.segments`, `PhraseStructure.Includes`, `PhraseStructure.Excludes`,
  `PhraseStructure.Contains`: the segments of a category and what it dominates.
* `PhraseStructure.IsMaximalCategory`, `PhraseStructure.maximalProjections`,
  `PhraseStructure.maxCommand`: maximal categories and MAX-command from them.
* `PhraseStructure.headDaughterRel`, `PhraseStructure.maximalProjectionAt`,
  `PhraseStructure.projectionIndex`, `PhraseStructure.adjunctionIndex`: head relations from
  head-daughter indices on tree positions.

## Main results

* `PhraseStructure.isLeast_projections_iff`, `PhraseStructure.exists_isLeast_projections`: the
  maximal projection of a node is the least of its projections, and it exists.
* `PhraseStructure.isChain_segments`, `PhraseStructure.includes_iff`,
  `PhraseStructure.excludes_iff`: the segments of a category form a chain, so inclusion is decided
  at the lowest segment and exclusion at the top.
* `PhraseStructure.not_includes_of_covBy`, `PhraseStructure.maxCommand_adjunct`: an adjunct is not
  included in the category it adjoins to, and it MAX-commands out of it.
* `PhraseStructure.mem_maxCommand_iff_le`: the MAX-command domain of a node that projects further
  is the cone of the lowest segment of its maximal category.
* `PhraseStructure.IsLexicalHeadOf.unique`: along a functional head relation a node has one lexical
  head.
* `PhraseStructure.isLeast_maximalProjectionAt`: `maximalProjectionAt` computes the maximal
  projection.

## Implementation notes

A minimal projection is a node with no head daughter, so on a tree whose phrases are not all
headed, an exocentric node is minimal as well; on an endocentric tree the minimal projections are
the leaves. A leaf that is not its mother's head daughter, such as a pronoun standing for a noun
phrase, is minimal and maximal at once. Lasnik and Saito's alternative, on which adjunction makes
a further maximal projection, is node-level maximality `IsMaximalProjection P` on the same
relations.

## References

* [barker-pullum-1990]
* [may-1985]
* [chomsky-1986]
* [chomsky-1995]
* [chomsky-2013]
* [lasnik-saito-1992]
* [pollard-sag-1994]
* [kay-fillmore-1999]
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace PhraseStructure

section Defs

variable {α : Type*} (H : α → α → Prop)

/-- `IsProjectionOf H h p` says that `p` is a projection of `h`, that is, `h` is reached from `p`
through head daughters. -/
def IsProjectionOf (h p : α) : Prop := Relation.ReflTransGen H p h

/-- A node is a maximal projection when it projects no further, being no node's head daughter. -/
def IsMaximalProjection (p : α) : Prop := ∀ m, ¬ H m p

/-- A node is a minimal projection when it is no projection, having no head daughter. -/
def IsMinimalProjection (p : α) : Prop := ∀ d, ¬ H p d

/-- `h` is the lexical head of `p` when `p` projects from `h` and `h` is a minimal projection. -/
def IsLexicalHeadOf (h p : α) : Prop := IsProjectionOf H h p ∧ IsMinimalProjection H h

variable {H}

@[refl] theorem IsProjectionOf.refl (h : α) : IsProjectionOf H h h := Relation.ReflTransGen.refl

theorem IsProjectionOf.head {h m d : α} (hmd : H m d) (hd : IsProjectionOf H h d) :
    IsProjectionOf H h m :=
  Relation.ReflTransGen.head hmd hd

theorem IsProjectionOf.trans {h p q : α} (hp : IsProjectionOf H h p) (hq : IsProjectionOf H p q) :
    IsProjectionOf H h q :=
  Relation.ReflTransGen.trans hq hp

theorem isProjectionOf_iff_eq_or {h p : α} :
    IsProjectionOf H h p ↔ p = h ∨ ∃ d, H p d ∧ IsProjectionOf H h d :=
  Relation.ReflTransGen.cases_head_iff

theorem IsMaximalProjection.eq_of_isProjectionOf {h p : α} (hp : IsMaximalProjection H p)
    (hph : IsProjectionOf H p h) : h = p := by
  rcases Relation.ReflTransGen.cases_tail hph with rfl | ⟨c, _, hcp⟩
  · rfl
  · exact absurd hcp (hp c)

/-- Along a functional head relation a node has one lexical head. -/
theorem IsLexicalHeadOf.unique (hfun : Relator.RightUnique H) {p h h' : α}
    (hh : IsLexicalHeadOf H h p) (hh' : IsLexicalHeadOf H h' p) : h = h' := by
  rcases Relation.ReflTransGen.total_of_right_unique hfun hh.1 hh'.1 with h1 | h1
  · rcases Relation.ReflTransGen.cases_head h1 with rfl | ⟨c, hc, _⟩
    · rfl
    · exact absurd hc (hh.2 c)
  · rcases Relation.ReflTransGen.cases_head h1 with rfl | ⟨c, hc, _⟩
    · rfl
    · exact absurd hc (hh'.2 c)

end Defs

section Order

variable {α : Type*} [PartialOrder α] (H : α → α → Prop)

variable {H} (hH : ∀ m d, H m d → m ⋖ d)
include hH

theorem IsProjectionOf.le {h p : α} (hp : IsProjectionOf H h p) : p ≤ h := by
  induction hp with
  | refl => exact le_rfl
  | tail _ hbc ih => exact ih.trans (hH _ _ hbc).le

theorem IsProjectionOf.of_le_of_le [IsLeftLinear α] {h p x : α} (hp : IsProjectionOf H h p)
    (hpx : p ≤ x) (hxh : x ≤ h) : IsProjectionOf H h x := by
  induction hp using Relation.ReflTransGen.head_induction_on with
  | refl => exact (le_antisymm hxh hpx) ▸ .refl _
  | @head p d hpd hdh ih =>
    rcases eq_or_lt_of_le hpx with rfl | hlt
    · exact .head hpd hdh
    · have hdx : d ≤ x := by
        rcases IsLeftLinear.comparable_of_le_common (IsProjectionOf.le hH hdh) hxh with h | h
        · exact h
        · exact (eq_or_lt_of_le h).elim (fun e ↦ e ▸ le_rfl) fun hxd ↦
            absurd hxd ((hH _ _ hpd).2 hlt)
      exact ih hdx

theorem IsProjectionOf.reflTransGen_of_le [IsLeftLinear α] {h p q : α}
    (hp : IsProjectionOf H h p) (hq : IsProjectionOf H h q) (hpq : p ≤ q) :
    Relation.ReflTransGen H p q := by
  induction hp using Relation.ReflTransGen.head_induction_on with
  | refl => exact (le_antisymm (hq.le hH) hpq) ▸ .refl
  | @head p d hpd hdh ih =>
    rcases eq_or_lt_of_le hpq with rfl | hlt
    · exact .refl
    · refine .head hpd (ih ?_)
      rcases IsLeftLinear.comparable_of_le_common (IsProjectionOf.le hH hdh) (hq.le hH) with h | h
      · exact h
      · exact (eq_or_lt_of_le h).elim (fun e ↦ e ▸ le_rfl) fun hqd ↦
          absurd hqd ((hH _ _ hpd).2 hlt)

theorem IsProjectionOf.exists_of_lt [IsLeftLinear α] {h p q : α} (hp : IsProjectionOf H h p)
    (hq : IsProjectionOf H h q) (hpq : p < q) : ∃ m, H m q := by
  rcases Relation.ReflTransGen.cases_tail (hp.reflTransGen_of_le hH hq hpq.le) with
    rfl | ⟨m, _, hm⟩
  · exact absurd rfl hpq.ne
  · exact ⟨m, hm⟩

/-- The maximal projection of `h` is the least of its projections. -/
theorem isLeast_projections_iff [IsLeftLinear α] {h m : α} :
    IsLeast {p | IsProjectionOf H h p} m ↔ IsProjectionOf H h m ∧ IsMaximalProjection H m := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨hm, hmin⟩
    exact ⟨hm, fun x hxm ↦ (hH _ _ hxm).lt.not_ge (hmin (hm.head hxm))⟩
  · rintro ⟨hm, hmax⟩
    refine ⟨hm, fun p hp ↦ ?_⟩
    rcases IsLeftLinear.comparable_of_le_common (hp.le hH) (hm.le hH) with h | h
    · rcases eq_or_lt_of_le h with rfl | hlt
      · exact le_rfl
      · obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hp.exists_of_lt hH hm hlt
        exact absurd hx (hmax x)
    · exact h

/-- Every node has a maximal projection. -/
theorem exists_isLeast_projections [IsLeftLinear α] [WellFoundedLT α] (h : α) :
    ∃ m, IsLeast {p | IsProjectionOf H h p} m := by
  obtain ⟨m, hm, hmin⟩ := WellFounded.has_min wellFounded_lt {p | IsProjectionOf H h p}
    ⟨h, .refl h⟩
  refine ⟨m, hm, fun p hp ↦ ?_⟩
  rcases IsLeftLinear.comparable_of_le_common (hp.le hH) (hm.le hH) with h' | h'
  · exact (eq_or_lt_of_le h').elim (fun e ↦ e.symm.le) fun hlt ↦ absurd hlt (hmin p hp)
  · exact h'

end Order

/-! ### Segments and categories

An adjunction relation `A`, with `A m d` saying that `m` is the segment of a category immediately
above its host `d`, groups nodes into categories: the segments of a category are the nodes joined
by adjunction steps. A category dominates what every one of its segments dominates and excludes
what none of them dominates; the segments of a category form a chain, so domination by the
category is domination by its lowest segment. -/

section Segments

variable {α : Type*} (A : α → α → Prop)

/-- The segments of the category of `x` are the nodes joined to `x` by adjunction steps. -/
def segments (x : α) : Set α := {y | Relation.EqvGen A x y}

variable {A}

@[simp] theorem mem_segments_self (x : α) : x ∈ segments A x := Relation.EqvGen.refl x

theorem mem_segments_comm {x y : α} : y ∈ segments A x ↔ x ∈ segments A y :=
  ⟨Relation.EqvGen.symm _ _, Relation.EqvGen.symm _ _⟩

theorem segments_eq_of_mem {x y : α} (h : y ∈ segments A x) : segments A y = segments A x :=
  Set.ext fun _ ↦ ⟨fun hz ↦ Relation.EqvGen.trans _ _ _ h hz,
    fun hz ↦ Relation.EqvGen.trans _ _ _ (Relation.EqvGen.symm _ _ h) hz⟩

theorem mem_segments_of_reflTransGen {x y : α} (h : Relation.ReflTransGen A x y) :
    y ∈ segments A x := by
  induction h with
  | refl => exact mem_segments_self x
  | tail _ hbc ih => exact Relation.EqvGen.trans _ _ _ ih (Relation.EqvGen.rel _ _ hbc)

@[simp] theorem segments_bot (x : α) : segments (⊥ : α → α → Prop) x = {x} := by
  ext y
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ ?_, fun h ↦ by rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff.1 h]; exact mem_segments_self x⟩
  induction h with
  | rel _ _ h => exact h.elim
  | refl => rfl
  | symm _ _ _ ih => exact ih.symm
  | trans _ _ _ _ _ ih₁ ih₂ => exact ih₂.trans ih₁

variable [PartialOrder α] (A)

/-- The category of `x` includes `y` when every segment of it dominates `y`. -/
def Includes (x y : α) : Prop := ∀ s ∈ segments A x, s ≤ y

/-- The category of `x` excludes `y` when no segment of it dominates `y`. -/
def Excludes (x y : α) : Prop := ∀ s ∈ segments A x, ¬ s ≤ y

/-- The category of `x` contains `y` when some segment of it dominates `y`. -/
def Contains (x y : α) : Prop := ∃ s ∈ segments A x, s ≤ y

variable {A}

theorem Includes.contains {x y : α} (h : Includes A x y) : Contains A x y :=
  ⟨x, mem_segments_self x, h x (mem_segments_self x)⟩

theorem not_excludes_iff_contains {x y : α} : ¬ Excludes A x y ↔ Contains A x y := by
  simp [Excludes, Contains]

theorem includes_congr {x x' y : α} (h : x' ∈ segments A x) :
    Includes A x' y ↔ Includes A x y := by
  simp only [Includes, segments_eq_of_mem h]

theorem excludes_congr {x x' y : α} (h : x' ∈ segments A x) :
    Excludes A x' y ↔ Excludes A x y := by
  simp only [Excludes, segments_eq_of_mem h]

@[simp] theorem includes_bot {x y : α} : Includes (⊥ : α → α → Prop) x y ↔ x ≤ y := by
  simp [Includes]

@[simp] theorem excludes_bot {x y : α} : Excludes (⊥ : α → α → Prop) x y ↔ ¬ x ≤ y := by
  simp [Excludes]

theorem contains_of_covBy {m a : α} (ha : m ⋖ a) : Contains A m a :=
  ⟨m, mem_segments_self m, ha.lt.le⟩

theorem eq_of_covBy_covBy [IsLeftLinear α] {m m' d : α} (hm : m ⋖ d) (hm' : m' ⋖ d) :
    m = m' := by
  rcases IsLeftLinear.comparable_of_le_common hm.le hm'.le with h | h
  · exact (eq_or_lt_of_le h).elim id fun hlt ↦ absurd hm'.lt (hm.2 hlt).elim
  · exact ((eq_or_lt_of_le h).elim Eq.symm fun hlt ↦ absurd hm.lt (hm'.2 hlt).elim)

theorem not_le_of_covBy {m a d : α} (ha : m ⋖ a) (hd : m ⋖ d) (had : a ≠ d) : ¬ a ≤ d :=
  fun h ↦ had ((hd.eq_or_eq ha.lt.le h).resolve_left (ne_of_gt ha.lt))

variable (hA : ∀ m d, A m d → m ⋖ d)
include hA

theorem leftUnique_of_covBy [IsLeftLinear α] : Relator.LeftUnique A :=
  fun _ _ _ hm hm' ↦ eq_of_covBy_covBy (hA _ _ hm) (hA _ _ hm')

theorem mem_segments_iff [IsLeftLinear α] (hU : Relator.RightUnique A) {x y : α} :
    y ∈ segments A x ↔ Relation.ReflTransGen A x y ∨ Relation.ReflTransGen A y x := by
  have hL : Relator.RightUnique (Function.swap A) := fun _ _ _ h h' ↦
    leftUnique_of_covBy hA h h'
  constructor
  · intro h
    induction h with
    | rel _ _ h => exact .inl (.single h)
    | refl => exact .inl .refl
    | symm _ _ _ ih => exact ih.symm
    | trans a b c _ _ ih₁ ih₂ =>
      rcases ih₁ with h₁ | h₁ <;> rcases ih₂ with h₂ | h₂
      · exact .inl (h₁.trans h₂)
      · rcases Relation.ReflTransGen.total_of_right_unique hL
          (Relation.reflTransGen_swap.2 h₁) (Relation.reflTransGen_swap.2 h₂) with h | h
        · exact .inr (Relation.reflTransGen_swap.1 h)
        · exact .inl (Relation.reflTransGen_swap.1 h)
      · exact Relation.ReflTransGen.total_of_right_unique hU h₁ h₂
      · exact .inr (h₂.trans h₁)
  · rintro (h | h)
    · exact mem_segments_of_reflTransGen h
    · exact mem_segments_comm.1 (mem_segments_of_reflTransGen h)

/-- The segments of a category form a chain. -/
theorem isChain_segments [IsLeftLinear α] (hU : Relator.RightUnique A) (x : α) :
    IsChain (· ≤ ·) (segments A x) := by
  have hL : Relator.RightUnique (Function.swap A) := fun _ _ _ h h' ↦
    leftUnique_of_covBy hA h h'
  intro y hy z hz _
  rcases (mem_segments_iff hA hU).1 hy with hy | hy <;>
    rcases (mem_segments_iff hA hU).1 hz with hz | hz
  · exact (Relation.ReflTransGen.total_of_right_unique hU hy hz).imp
      (IsProjectionOf.le hA ·) (IsProjectionOf.le hA ·)
  · exact .inr ((IsProjectionOf.le hA hz).trans (IsProjectionOf.le hA hy))
  · exact .inl ((IsProjectionOf.le hA hy).trans (IsProjectionOf.le hA hz))
  · exact (Relation.ReflTransGen.total_of_right_unique hL (Relation.reflTransGen_swap.2 hy)
      (Relation.reflTransGen_swap.2 hz)).symm.imp
      (fun h ↦ IsProjectionOf.le hA (Relation.reflTransGen_swap.1 h))
      (fun h ↦ IsProjectionOf.le hA (Relation.reflTransGen_swap.1 h))

/-- A category includes what the segments at or below `x` dominate, since those above dominate
whatever `x` does. -/
theorem includes_iff [IsLeftLinear α] (hU : Relator.RightUnique A) {x y : α} :
    Includes A x y ↔ ∀ s, Relation.ReflTransGen A x s → s ≤ y := by
  refine ⟨fun h s hs ↦ h s (mem_segments_of_reflTransGen hs), fun h s hs ↦ ?_⟩
  rcases (mem_segments_iff hA hU).1 hs with hs | hs
  · exact h s hs
  · exact (IsProjectionOf.le hA hs).trans (h x .refl)

/-- A category excludes what no segment at or above `x` dominates. -/
theorem excludes_iff [IsLeftLinear α] (hU : Relator.RightUnique A) {x y : α} :
    Excludes A x y ↔ ∀ s, Relation.ReflTransGen A s x → ¬ s ≤ y := by
  refine ⟨fun h s hs ↦ h s (mem_segments_comm.1 (mem_segments_of_reflTransGen hs)),
    fun h s hs hsy ↦ ?_⟩
  rcases (mem_segments_iff hA hU).1 hs with hs | hs
  · exact h x .refl ((IsProjectionOf.le hA hs).trans hsy)
  · exact h s hs hsy

theorem includes_iff_forall_le [IsLeftLinear α] (hU : Relator.RightUnique A) {x y : α} :
    Includes A x y ↔ x ≤ y ∧ ∀ q, Relation.ReflTransGen A x q → q ≤ y → ∀ d, A q d → d ≤ y := by
  rw [includes_iff hA hU]
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ ⟨h x .refl, fun q hq _ d hqd ↦ h d (hq.tail hqd)⟩, fun ⟨hxy, h⟩ s hs ↦ ?_⟩
  induction hs with
  | refl => exact hxy
  | tail hq hqd ih => exact h _ hq ih _ hqd

/-- An adjunct is not included in the category it adjoins to, since the host segment does not
dominate it. -/
theorem not_includes_of_covBy {m d a : α} (hmd : A m d) (ha : m ⋖ a) (had : a ≠ d) :
    ¬ Includes A m a := fun h ↦
  not_le_of_covBy (hA _ _ hmd) ha had.symm (h d (Relation.EqvGen.rel _ _ hmd))

end Segments

/-! ### Maximal categories and MAX-command

With projection `P` and adjunction `A` the head relation is `P ⊔ A`. A category is maximal when no
segment of it projects further, and MAX-command is generated by the maximal categories, each read
at its lowest segment, the one whose domination is the category's. Without adjunction these are
the maximal projections. -/

section Categories

variable {α : Type*} (P A : α → α → Prop)

/-- A category is maximal when none of its segments projects further. -/
def IsMaximalCategory (x : α) : Prop := ∀ s ∈ segments A x, IsMaximalProjection P s

/-- The maximal projections, which generate MAX-command, are the lowest segments of the maximal
categories. -/
def maximalProjections : Set α := {x | IsMinimalProjection A x ∧ IsMaximalCategory P A x}

variable {P A}

theorem isMaximalCategory_congr {x x' : α} (h : x' ∈ segments A x) :
    IsMaximalCategory P A x' ↔ IsMaximalCategory P A x := by
  simp only [IsMaximalCategory, segments_eq_of_mem h]

theorem IsMaximalCategory.isMaximalProjection {x : α} (h : IsMaximalCategory P A x) :
    IsMaximalProjection P x := h x (mem_segments_self x)

@[simp] theorem isMaximalCategory_bot {x : α} :
    IsMaximalCategory P (⊥ : α → α → Prop) x ↔ IsMaximalProjection P x := by
  simp [IsMaximalCategory]

@[simp] theorem maximalProjections_bot :
    maximalProjections P (⊥ : α → α → Prop) = {x | IsMaximalProjection P x} := by
  ext x; simp [maximalProjections, IsMinimalProjection]

theorem eq_of_reflTransGen_sup {b x : α} (hb : IsMinimalProjection A b)
    (hbx : Relation.ReflTransGen (P ⊔ A) b x) (hx : IsMaximalCategory P A x) : x = b := by
  induction hbx with
  | refl => rfl
  | @tail c x _ hcx ih =>
    rcases hcx with hcx | hcx
    · exact absurd hcx (hx.isMaximalProjection c)
    · have hc : IsMaximalCategory P A c :=
        (isMaximalCategory_congr (mem_segments_comm.1 (Relation.EqvGen.rel _ _ hcx))).2 hx
      exact absurd (ih hc ▸ hcx) (hb x)

variable [PartialOrder α]

variable (P A) in
/-- MAX-command is generated by the maximal categories. -/
abbrev maxCommand : SetRel α α := commandRelation (maximalProjections P A)

variable (hA : ∀ m d, A m d → m ⋖ d)
include hA

/-- An adjunct to a maximal category MAX-commands out of it, while what the category dominates
does not MAX-command the adjunct. -/
theorem maxCommand_adjunct [IsLeftLinear α] {m d a b : α} (hmd : A m d) (ha : m ⋖ a)
    (had : a ≠ d) (hd : d ∈ maximalProjections P A) (hdb : d < b) :
    (a, b) ∈ maxCommand P A ∧ (b, a) ∉ maxCommand P A :=
  ⟨mem_commandRelation_of_covBy ha ((hA _ _ hmd).lt.le.trans hdb.le), fun h ↦
    not_le_of_covBy (hA _ _ hmd) ha had.symm (h hd hdb)⟩

theorem isMaximalCategory_iff_forall_above [IsLeftLinear α] (hP : ∀ m d, P m d → m ⋖ d)
    (hU : Relator.RightUnique A) (hdisj : ∀ m d, A m d → ¬ P m d) {x : α} :
    IsMaximalCategory P A x ↔ ∀ s, Relation.ReflTransGen A s x → IsMaximalProjection P s := by
  refine ⟨fun h s hs ↦ h s (mem_segments_comm.1 (mem_segments_of_reflTransGen hs)),
    fun h s hs ↦ ?_⟩
  rcases (mem_segments_iff hA hU).1 hs with hs | hs
  · rcases Relation.ReflTransGen.cases_tail hs with rfl | ⟨c, -, hcs⟩
    · exact h s .refl
    · exact fun m hm ↦ hdisj c s hcs (eq_of_covBy_covBy (hP _ _ hm) (hA _ _ hcs) ▸ hm)
  · exact h s hs

/-- A node that projects to the lowest segment `b` of a maximal category MAX-commands exactly what
`b` dominates. -/
theorem mem_maxCommand_iff_le [IsLeftLinear α] (hP : ∀ m d, P m d → m ⋖ d) {h b x : α}
    (hb : IsProjectionOf (P ⊔ A) h b) (hmax : b ∈ maximalProjections P A) (hne : b ≠ h) :
    (h, x) ∈ maxCommand P A ↔ b ≤ x := by
  have hH : ∀ m d, (P ⊔ A) m d → m ⋖ d := fun m d hmd ↦ hmd.elim (hP m d) (hA m d)
  refine mem_commandRelation_iff_le ⟨⟨hmax, lt_of_le_of_ne (hb.le hH) hne⟩, fun x ⟨hx, hxh⟩ ↦ ?_⟩
  rcases IsLeftLinear.comparable_of_le_common hxh.le (hb.le hH) with h' | h'
  · exact h'
  · rcases eq_or_lt_of_le h' with rfl | hlt
    · exact le_rfl
    · exact absurd (eq_of_reflTransGen_sup hmax.1
        (hb.reflTransGen_of_le hH (hb.of_le_of_le hH hlt.le hxh.le) hlt.le) hx.2) hlt.ne'

end Categories

/-! ### Head daughters at tree positions -/

section Positions

open Core.Order

variable (hd : TreePath → Option ℕ)

/-- `headDaughterRel hd m d` says that `d` is the daughter of `m` at the index `hd m`. -/
def headDaughterRel (m d : TreePath) : Prop := ∃ i, hd m = some i ∧ d.toList = m.toList ++ [i]

instance : DecidableRel (headDaughterRel hd) := fun m d ↦
  match h : hd m with
  | none => isFalse (by rintro ⟨i, hi, -⟩; rw [h] at hi; cases hi)
  | some i => decidable_of_iff (d.toList = m.toList ++ [i])
      ⟨fun hd' ↦ ⟨i, h, hd'⟩, fun ⟨j, hj, hd'⟩ ↦ by rw [h] at hj; cases hj; exact hd'⟩

theorem headDaughterRel_covBy {m d : TreePath} (h : headDaughterRel hd m d) : m ⋖ d :=
  TreePath.covBy_iff.2 ⟨h.choose, h.choose_spec.2⟩

theorem headDaughterRel_rightUnique : Relator.RightUnique (headDaughterRel hd) := by
  rintro m d d' ⟨i, hi, hd⟩ ⟨j, hj, hd'⟩
  rw [hi] at hj
  cases hj
  exact TreePath.ext (hd.trans hd'.symm)

theorem isMinimalProjection_headDaughterRel_iff {p : TreePath} :
    IsMinimalProjection (headDaughterRel hd) p ↔ hd p = none := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    cases hp : hd p with
    | none => rfl
    | some i => exact absurd ⟨i, hp, rfl⟩ (h ⟨p.toList ++ [i]⟩)
  · rintro h d ⟨i, hi, -⟩
    rw [h] at hi
    cases hi

instance (p : TreePath) : Decidable (IsMinimalProjection (headDaughterRel hd) p) :=
  decidable_of_iff _ (isMinimalProjection_headDaughterRel_iff hd).symm

theorem isMaximalProjection_headDaughterRel_iff {p : TreePath} :
    IsMaximalProjection (headDaughterRel hd) p ↔ ¬ headDaughterRel hd p.parent p := by
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ h _, fun h m hm ↦ h ?_⟩
  obtain rfl : m = p.parent := by
    obtain ⟨i, -, hi⟩ := hm
    exact TreePath.ext (by simp [hi])
  exact hm

instance (p : TreePath) : Decidable (IsMaximalProjection (headDaughterRel hd) p) :=
  decidable_of_iff _ (isMaximalProjection_headDaughterRel_iff hd).symm

theorem isProjectionOf_headDaughterRel_iff {h p : TreePath} :
    IsProjectionOf (headDaughterRel hd) h p ↔
      p ≤ h ∧ ∀ q ∈ h.toList.inits.map TreePath.mk, p < q → headDaughterRel hd q.parent q := by
  have hH : ∀ m d, headDaughterRel hd m d → m ⋖ d := fun _ _ ↦ headDaughterRel_covBy hd
  constructor
  · intro hp
    refine ⟨hp.le hH, fun q hq hpq ↦ ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨l, hl, rfl⟩ := List.mem_map.mp hq
    have hqh : (⟨l⟩ : TreePath) ≤ h := TreePath.le_def.mpr ((List.mem_inits _ _).mp hl)
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := hp.exists_of_lt hH (hp.of_le_of_le hH hpq.le hqh) hpq
    have : m = TreePath.parent ⟨l⟩ := by
      obtain ⟨i, -, hi⟩ := hm
      have hi' : l = m.toList ++ [i] := hi
      exact TreePath.ext (by rw [TreePath.parent_toList, hi', List.dropLast_concat])
    exact this ▸ hm
  · rintro ⟨hph, hall⟩
    obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := TreePath.le_def.mp hph
    obtain ⟨p⟩ := p
    obtain ⟨h⟩ := h
    simp only at hs
    subst hs
    suffices key : ∀ s, (∀ q ∈ (p ++ s).inits.map TreePath.mk, (⟨p⟩ : TreePath) < q →
        headDaughterRel hd q.parent q) → IsProjectionOf (headDaughterRel hd) ⟨p ++ s⟩ ⟨p⟩ from
      key s hall
    intro s
    induction s using List.reverseRecOn with
    | nil => intro _; simpa using IsProjectionOf.refl (H := headDaughterRel hd) ⟨p⟩
    | append_singleton s i ih =>
      intro hall
      rw [← List.append_assoc] at hall ⊢
      refine Relation.ReflTransGen.tail (ih fun q hq hpq ↦ hall q ?_ hpq) ?_
      · obtain ⟨l, hl, rfl⟩ := List.mem_map.mp hq
        exact List.mem_map.mpr ⟨l, (List.mem_inits _ _).mpr
          (((List.mem_inits _ _).mp hl).trans (List.prefix_append _ _)), rfl⟩
      · have hlt : (⟨p⟩ : TreePath) < ⟨p ++ s ++ [i]⟩ :=
          lt_of_le_of_ne (TreePath.le_def.mpr (by simp)) fun e ↦ by
            simpa using congrArg (fun q : TreePath ↦ q.toList.length) e
        have := hall ⟨p ++ s ++ [i]⟩
          (List.mem_map.mpr ⟨_, (List.mem_inits _ _).mpr List.prefix_rfl, rfl⟩) hlt
        have hpar : (⟨p ++ s ++ [i]⟩ : TreePath).parent = ⟨p ++ s⟩ := TreePath.ext (by simp)
        rwa [hpar] at this

instance (h p : TreePath) : Decidable (IsProjectionOf (headDaughterRel hd) h p) :=
  decidable_of_iff _ (isProjectionOf_headDaughterRel_iff hd).symm

/-- The maximal projection of `h` is its shortest prefix that is a projection of it. -/
def maximalProjectionAt (h : TreePath) : TreePath :=
  ⟨(h.toList.inits.find? fun r ↦ decide (IsProjectionOf (headDaughterRel hd) h ⟨r⟩)).getD
    h.toList⟩

theorem maximalProjectionAt_le (h : TreePath) : maximalProjectionAt hd h ≤ h := by
  unfold maximalProjectionAt
  cases hf : h.toList.inits.find? _ with
  | none => exact le_rfl
  | some r => exact TreePath.le_def.2 ((List.mem_inits _ _).1 (List.mem_of_find?_eq_some hf))

theorem isProjectionOf_maximalProjectionAt (h : TreePath) :
    IsProjectionOf (headDaughterRel hd) h (maximalProjectionAt hd h) := by
  unfold maximalProjectionAt
  cases hf : h.toList.inits.find? _ with
  | none => exact .refl _
  | some r => simpa using List.find?_some hf

/-- `maximalProjectionAt hd h` is the least projection of `h`. -/
theorem isLeast_maximalProjectionAt (h : TreePath) :
    IsLeast {p | IsProjectionOf (headDaughterRel hd) h p} (maximalProjectionAt hd h) := by
  refine ⟨isProjectionOf_maximalProjectionAt hd h, fun p hp ↦ ?_⟩
  have hH : ∀ m d, headDaughterRel hd m d → m ⋖ d := fun _ _ ↦ headDaughterRel_covBy hd
  have hmem : p.toList ∈ h.toList.inits := (List.mem_inits _ _).2 (TreePath.le_def.1 (hp.le hH))
  unfold maximalProjectionAt
  cases hf : h.toList.inits.find? _ with
  | none =>
    exact absurd (by simpa using hp) ((List.find?_eq_none.1 hf) p.toList hmem)
  | some r =>
    obtain ⟨-, as, bs, hl, has⟩ := List.find?_eq_some_iff_append.1 hf
    have hpw := List.pairwise_inits h.toList
    rw [hl, List.pairwise_append, List.pairwise_cons] at hpw
    rw [hl] at hmem
    rcases List.mem_append.1 hmem with hm | hm
    · exact absurd (by simpa using hp) (by simpa using has _ hm)
    · rcases List.mem_cons.1 hm with rfl | hm
      · exact le_rfl
      · exact TreePath.le_def.2 (hpw.2.1.1 _ hm)

/-! #### Projection and adjunction at positions -/

variable (seg : TreePath → Prop) [DecidablePred seg]

/-- The head daughter of a position that is not a segment, a projection step. -/
def projectionIndex (p : TreePath) : Option ℕ := if seg p then none else hd p

/-- The head daughter of a segment, its host. -/
def adjunctionIndex (p : TreePath) : Option ℕ := if seg p then hd p else none

theorem headDaughterRel_eq_sup :
    headDaughterRel hd =
      headDaughterRel (projectionIndex hd seg) ⊔ headDaughterRel (adjunctionIndex hd seg) := by
  ext m d
  simp only [headDaughterRel, projectionIndex, adjunctionIndex, Pi.sup_apply]
  by_cases h : seg m <;> simp [h]

theorem not_projection_of_adjunction {m d : TreePath}
    (h : headDaughterRel (adjunctionIndex hd seg) m d) :
    ¬ headDaughterRel (projectionIndex hd seg) m d := by
  obtain ⟨i, hi, -⟩ := h
  rintro ⟨j, hj, -⟩
  simp only [adjunctionIndex, projectionIndex] at hi hj
  split at hi <;> simp_all

theorem isMaximalCategory_iff_inits (x : TreePath) :
    IsMaximalCategory (headDaughterRel (projectionIndex hd seg))
        (headDaughterRel (adjunctionIndex hd seg)) x ↔
      ∀ s ∈ x.toList.inits.map TreePath.mk,
        IsProjectionOf (headDaughterRel (adjunctionIndex hd seg)) x s →
          IsMaximalProjection (headDaughterRel (projectionIndex hd seg)) s := by
  rw [isMaximalCategory_iff_forall_above (fun _ _ ↦ headDaughterRel_covBy _)
    (fun _ _ ↦ headDaughterRel_covBy _) (headDaughterRel_rightUnique _)
    (fun _ _ ↦ not_projection_of_adjunction hd seg)]
  constructor
  · exact fun h s _ hs ↦ h s hs
  · exact fun h s hs ↦ h s (List.mem_map.2 ⟨_, (List.mem_inits _ _).2
      (TreePath.le_def.1 (IsProjectionOf.le (fun _ _ ↦ headDaughterRel_covBy _) hs)), rfl⟩) hs

instance (x : TreePath) : Decidable (IsMaximalCategory (headDaughterRel (projectionIndex hd seg))
    (headDaughterRel (adjunctionIndex hd seg)) x) :=
  decidable_of_iff _ (isMaximalCategory_iff_inits hd seg x).symm

instance (x : TreePath) :
    Decidable (x ∈ maximalProjections (headDaughterRel (projectionIndex hd seg))
      (headDaughterRel (adjunctionIndex hd seg))) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Decidable (_ ∧ _))

theorem includes_iff_inits (x y : TreePath) :
    Includes (headDaughterRel (adjunctionIndex hd seg)) x y ↔
      x ≤ y ∧ ∀ q ∈ y.toList.inits.map TreePath.mk,
        IsProjectionOf (headDaughterRel (adjunctionIndex hd seg)) q x →
          ∀ i, adjunctionIndex hd seg q = some i → (⟨q.toList ++ [i]⟩ : TreePath) ≤ y := by
  rw [includes_iff_forall_le (fun _ _ ↦ headDaughterRel_covBy _) (headDaughterRel_rightUnique _)]
  refine and_congr_right fun _ ↦ ⟨fun h q hqy hq i hi ↦ h q hq ?_ _ ⟨i, hi, rfl⟩,
    fun h q hq hqy d ⟨i, hi, hd'⟩ ↦ ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨l, hl, rfl⟩ := List.mem_map.1 hqy
    exact TreePath.le_def.2 ((List.mem_inits _ _).1 hl)
  · have := h q (List.mem_map.2 ⟨_, (List.mem_inits _ _).2 (TreePath.le_def.1 hqy), rfl⟩) hq i hi
    exact TreePath.ext hd' ▸ this

instance (x y : TreePath) : Decidable (Includes (headDaughterRel (adjunctionIndex hd seg)) x y) :=
  decidable_of_iff _ (includes_iff_inits hd seg x y).symm

theorem excludes_iff_inits (x y : TreePath) :
    Excludes (headDaughterRel (adjunctionIndex hd seg)) x y ↔
      ∀ s ∈ x.toList.inits.map TreePath.mk,
        IsProjectionOf (headDaughterRel (adjunctionIndex hd seg)) x s → ¬ s ≤ y := by
  rw [excludes_iff (fun _ _ ↦ headDaughterRel_covBy _) (headDaughterRel_rightUnique _)]
  exact ⟨fun h s _ hs ↦ h s hs, fun h s hs ↦ h s (List.mem_map.2 ⟨_, (List.mem_inits _ _).2
    (TreePath.le_def.1 (IsProjectionOf.le (fun _ _ ↦ headDaughterRel_covBy _) hs)), rfl⟩) hs⟩

instance (x y : TreePath) : Decidable (Excludes (headDaughterRel (adjunctionIndex hd seg)) x y) :=
  decidable_of_iff _ (excludes_iff_inits hd seg x y).symm

instance (x y : TreePath) : Decidable (Contains (headDaughterRel (adjunctionIndex hd seg)) x y) :=
  decidable_of_iff _ not_excludes_iff_contains

end Positions

